        <mxCell id="legend" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;How to read this diagram&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color:#b85450&quot;&gt;PK&lt;/b&gt; primary key &amp;nbsp; &lt;b style=&quot;color:#6c8ebf&quot;&gt;FK&lt;/b&gt; foreign key &amp;nbsp; &lt;b style=&quot;color:#82b366&quot;&gt;UQ&lt;/b&gt; unique &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#999&quot;&gt;name?&lt;/span&gt; nullable &amp;nbsp; ▦ monthly-partitioned table&lt;br&gt;The grey footer row of a table lists standard columns: &lt;i&gt;tenant_id&lt;/i&gt; (owning school, enforced by row-level security on every tenant table), &lt;i&gt;created/updated_at&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;created/updated_by&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;deleted_at&lt;/i&gt; (soft delete), &lt;i&gt;version&lt;/i&gt; (optimistic lock).&lt;br&gt;Crow&#39;s-foot ends: the many side sits on the table holding the foreign key; a circle means optional.&lt;br&gt;Each module box lists which other modules it depends on. Every module also depends on &lt;b&gt;Tenancy&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;Reference Data&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;Identity&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;Platform&lt;/b&gt; (files), which are left out of the &quot;Depends on&quot; lines. On a module page, a foreign key to a table in another module is shown on its row as &lt;span style=&quot;color:#6c8ebf&quot;&gt;→ table&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;br&gt;Foreign keys between tenant tables are composite &lt;i&gt;(tenant_id, id)&lt;/i&gt;, so a row can never point at another school&#39;s data." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2784.5" width="1100" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
